BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pokemon-go-wild-area-2026-global@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T235103Z
SUMMARY:Pokémon GO Wild Area 2026: Global
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261115T180000
DESCRIPTION:GO Wild Area returns in 2026 with Steel- and Dragon-type Pokém
 on\, the debuts of Gigantamax Duraludon\, Dynamax Dialga\, and Dynamax Pal
 kia\, and powerful mighty Pokémon. Collect GO Safari Balls to help catch 
 these challenging encounters!\nDates: November 14 and 15\, 2026 Time: 10:0
 0 a.m. – 6:00 p.m. local time each day Location: Worldwide\nAll Trainers
  can participate in the global event. An optional US$11.99 ticket adds Spe
 cial Research\, increased Shiny chances\, extra Incense encounters\, and a
 dditional bonuses across both days. Purchase a ticket from the Pokémon GO
  Web Store.\n\n▸ Related Events\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n▸ Bonuses fo
 r All Trainers\nThe following bonuses apply from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. l
 ocal time on both event days.\n• Chance to get GO Safari Balls from Pok
 éStops and Gyms\n• Up to 3 free Raid Passes per day from Gyms\n• Dail
 y Max Particle collection limit increased to 1\,600\n• 3 GO Snapshot sur
 prise encounters per day\n• Party Play lasts for 8 hours\n• Chance to 
 encounter mighty Pokémon on Routes\nDaily Discoveries will be paused from
  November 9 at 12:01 a.m. through November 15\, 2026\, at 11:59 p.m. local
  time.\n\n▸ Additional Ticket Holder Bonuses\nThese benefits apply from 
 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. local time on both event days. The ticketed Raid P
 ass and Max Particle limits replace the free limits.\n• Increased chance
  to encounter Shiny Pokémon*\n• Daily Max Particle collection limit inc
 reased to 3\,200\n• Increased Max Particles from Power Spots and explora
 tion**\n• Up to 6 free Raid Passes per day from Gyms\n• GO Safari Ball
 s instead of Premier Balls for raids and Max Battles***\n• 2× Candy for
  catching Pokémon\n• 2× Incense duration\n• Increased chance of 10 k
 m Eggs from PokéStops and Gyms\n• 6 GO Snapshot surprise encounters per
  day\n• Lure Modules last for 2 hours\n*Shiny encounters are not guarant
 eed. **To use the increased exploration Max Particle bonus\, first collect
  all available Max Particles in the Nearby menu. Adventure Sync can help t
 rack exploration distance. ***GO Safari Balls replacing Premier Balls afte
 r raids and Max Battles is based on how ticketed GO Wild Area events worke
 d in previous years and is not yet confirmed.\n\n▸ Trading Bonuses\nTick
 et holders receive these benefits from 12:00 a.m. to 11:59 p.m. local time
  on both event days.\n• Up to 6 Special Trades per day\n• 1/2 Stardust
  cost for trades\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Gigantamax Duraludon Debut
 s\nGigantamax Duraludon makes its Pokémon GO debut at Pokémon GO Wild Ar
 ea! This larger-than-life Pokémon will appear in six-star Max Battles dur
 ing the event.\nTicket-holding Trainers can learn more about Gigantamax Du
 raludon in the event-exclusive Special Research story. Complete it for an 
 encounter with Gigantamax Duraludon with a Special Background!\nIf you’r
 e lucky\, you may encounter a Shiny one!\nPokémon: Gigantamax Duraludon\n
 \n▸ Dynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia\nDynamax Dialga and Dynamax Palkia
  make their Pokémon GO debuts during GO Wild Area 2026. Both can be Shiny
 !\nFor Global\, Dynamax Dialga appears on Saturday\, November 14\, and Dyn
 amax Palkia appears on Sunday\, November 15.\n\n▸ Private Dynamax Battle
  Groups\nStarting with GO Wild Area 2026\, Dynamax Battle lobbies offer Ba
 ttle to match automatically with other Trainers or Private Group to join a
 n existing group using its group code.\n\n▸ Adventure Effects in Battle 
 Lobbies\nStarting with Into the Wild\, select Adventure Effects can be act
 ivated while waiting in a raid or Max Battle lobby. Use Crowned Sword Zaci
 an’s Behemoth Blade or Crowned Shield Zamazenta’s Behemoth Bash Advent
 ure Effect before a Max Battle to help your group.\n\n▸ Machamp Wearing 
 a Modern Jacket\nA new costumed Machamp appears in three-star raids during
  the event. Lucky Trainers may encounter a Shiny one!\n\n▸ Special Backg
 rounds\nAfter a successful catch from raids or Max Battles\, Machamp weari
 ng a modern jacket\, Dynamax Dialga\, Dynamax Palkia\, Reshiram\, Zekrom\,
  Kyurem\, and Gigantamax Duraludon have a chance to have a new Special Bac
 kground.\n\n▸ Backgrounds on Your Trainer Profile\nYour buddy Pokémon
 ’s eligible Location Background or Special Background can now appear on 
 your Trainer profile\, where friends can see it too. Background support ro
 lls out on the following schedule:\n• November 6\, 2026\, at 10:00 a.m. 
 local time: GO Wild Area 2026 Location Backgrounds for Sendai and Mexico C
 ity.\n…\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Rotating Habitat Hours\nSteel- and 
 Dragon-themed encounters rotate hourly from 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. on bot
 h event days.\n\n▸ Solid as Steel Hour\n10:00 a.m. to 11:00 a.m. 12:00 p
 .m. to 1:00 p.m. 2:00 p.m. to 3:00 p.m. 4:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m.\nPokémon: 
 Alolan Sandshrew\, Alolan Diglett\, Magnemite\, Shellder\, Onix\, Porygon\
 , Shuckle\, Skarmory\, Nosepass\, Aron\, Beldum\, Piplup\, Shieldon\, Bron
 zor\, Lucario\, Drilbur\, Ferroseed\, Klink\, Galarian Stunfisk\, Durant\,
  Rookidee\, Tinkatink\n\n▸ Daring as Dragons Hour\n11:00 a.m. to 12:00 p
 .m. 1:00 p.m. to 2:00 p.m. 3:00 p.m. to 4:00 p.m. 5:00 p.m. to 6:00 p.m.\n
 Pokémon: Charmander\, Magikarp\, Dratini\, Gligar\, Trapinch\, Swablu\, B
 arboach\, Bagon\, Gible\, Tynamo\, Axew\, Heatmor\, Deino\, Skrelp\, Tyrun
 t\, Amaura\, Goomy\, Noibat\, Turtonator\, Jangmo-o\, Sizzlipede\, Frigiba
 x\n\n▸ Mighty Pokémon\nMighty Pokémon are more likely to have high Att
 ack\, Defense\, and HP ratings and be XL or XXL. They are harder to catch\
 , and some may be Shiny. GO Safari Balls improve your chances of catching 
 them.\nThe wild mighty Pokémon lineup changes each day. Mighty Pokémon r
 eportedly appear slightly more often in the last 15 minutes of each event 
 day\, from 5:45 p.m. to 6:00 p.m. local time.\n\n▸ Saturday\, November 1
 4\nPokémon: Alolan Exeggutor\, Scizor\, Flygon\, Walrein\, Metagross\, Em
 poleon\, Magnezone\, Conkeldurr\, Haxorus\n\n▸ Sunday\, November 15\nPok
 émon: Azumarill\, Kingdra\, Aggron\, Ferrothorn\, Hydreigon\, Goodra\, No
 ivern\, Tinkaton\, Clodsire\n\n▸ Incense Encounters\nAll Trainers can at
 tract these mighty Pokémon on both event days. These encounters exclude D
 aily Adventure Incense.\n…
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/pokemon-go-wild-area-2026-global/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:minior-showers-leonids-2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T235103Z
SUMMARY:Minior Showers: Leonids 2026
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261114T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261119T235900
DESCRIPTION:Explore by starlight during the Leonids meteor shower for a cha
 nce to encounter Minior in Pokémon GO!\nThis Minior Shower runs from Nove
 mber 14\, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. to November 19\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. local time
 .\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• Increased Stardust for catching Minior\n
 • Increased chance to encounter Minior from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local
  time each day\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Pokémon Debut\nMinior (Yell
 ow Core) will make its Pokémon GO debut during the Leonids meteor shower\
 , beginning November 14\, 2026\, at 5:00 p.m. local time!\nMinior (Green C
 ore) is reportedly also available in the wild during the Leonids.\nMinior 
 has seven different core colors: Red\, Orange\, Yellow\, Green\, Blue\, In
 digo\, and Violet. A different core color will debut during each of the si
 x meteor showers listed below. During the Geminids\, one core color will d
 ebut in the Northern Hemisphere and another in the Southern Hemisphere.\nP
 okémon: Minior (Yellow Core)\nGreen Core Minior debuted during the Orioni
 ds\, and Yellow Core Minior debuts during the Leonids. The core colors for
  the remaining meteor showers have not been announced.\n\n▸ Explore by S
 tarlight\nFrom 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time every day during each Min
 ior Shower\, shooting stars will light up the in-game sky. During these ho
 urs\, you’ll have an increased chance of encountering Minior in the wild
 !\n\n▸ Minior’s Form Changes\nMinior begins battles in its Meteor Form
 . When its health drops below 50%\, it changes form and exposes its core.\
 n• Meteor Form: Higher Defense and lower Attack.\n• Core exposed: High
 er Attack and lower Defense.\nInitially\, Minior will only be able to chan
 ge forms when battling Team GO Rocket\, team leaders\, or in the GO Battle
  League.\nMinior will not be eligible for the 2027 Latin America Internati
 onal Championships.\n\n▸ Annual Meteor Shower Schedule\nMinior can appea
 r during the following meteor showers each year. Each shower begins at 5:0
 0 p.m. on its first day and ends at 11:59 p.m. on its last day\, in local 
 time.\n• Orionids: October 19–24\, 2026\n• Leonids: November 14–19
 \, 2026\n• Geminids: December 11–16\, 2026\n• Eta Aquariids: May 3
 –8\, 2027\n• Southern Delta Aquariids: July 28–August 2\, 2027\n• 
 Perseids: August 10–15\, 2027\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounte
 rs\nYou may encounter Minior in its Meteor Form in the wild during the eve
 nt. You’ll receive 1\,000 Stardust for catching Minior.\nPokémon: Minio
 r (Meteor Form)\nMinior encounters are more likely from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 
 p.m. local time each day.\n\n━━ RESEARCH ━━\nNo Timed Research: Th
 ere is no Timed Research during the Leonids. The Minior Shower Timed Resea
 rch was only available during the Orionids\, the introductory event for Mi
 nior Showers.\n\n🔗 https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-leonids-2
 026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-leonids-2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
