BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:minior-showers-geminids-2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T235103Z
SUMMARY:Minior Showers: Geminids 2026
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261211T170000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261216T235900
DESCRIPTION:Explore by starlight during the Geminids meteor shower for a ch
 ance to encounter Minior in Pokémon GO!\nThis Minior Shower runs from Dec
 ember 11\, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. to December 16\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. local tim
 e.\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• Increased Stardust for catching Minior\n
 • Increased chance to encounter Minior from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local
  time each day\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Minior Cores\nMinior has sev
 en different core colors: Red\, Orange\, Yellow\, Green\, Blue\, Indigo\, 
 and Violet. A different core color will debut during each of the six meteo
 r showers listed below. During the Geminids\, one core color will debut in
  the Northern Hemisphere and another in the Southern Hemisphere.\nPokémon
 : Minior (Red Core)\, Minior (Orange Core)\, Minior (Yellow Core)\, Minior
  (Green Core)\, Minior (Blue Core)\, Minior (Indigo Core)\, Minior (Violet
  Core)\nGreen Core Minior debuted during the Orionids\, and Yellow Core Mi
 nior debuts during the Leonids. The core colors for the remaining meteor s
 howers have not been announced.\n\n▸ Explore by Starlight\nFrom 5:00 p.m
 . to 9:00 p.m. local time every day during each Minior Shower\, shooting s
 tars will light up the in-game sky. During these hours\, you’ll have an 
 increased chance of encountering Minior in the wild!\n\n▸ Minior’s For
 m Changes\nMinior begins battles in its Meteor Form. When its health drops
  below 50%\, it changes form and exposes its core.\n• Meteor Form: Highe
 r Defense and lower Attack.\n• Core exposed: Higher Attack and lower Def
 ense.\nInitially\, Minior will only be able to change forms when battling 
 Team GO Rocket\, team leaders\, or in the GO Battle League.\nMinior will n
 ot be eligible for the 2027 Latin America International Championships.\n\n
 ▸ Annual Meteor Shower Schedule\nMinior can appear during the following 
 meteor showers each year. Each shower begins at 5:00 p.m. on its first day
  and ends at 11:59 p.m. on its last day\, in local time.\n• Orionids: Oc
 tober 19–24\, 2026\n• Leonids: November 14–19\, 2026\n• Geminids: 
 December 11–16\, 2026\n• Eta Aquariids: May 3–8\, 2027\n• Southern
  Delta Aquariids: July 28–August 2\, 2027\n• Perseids: August 10–15\
 , 2027\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\n▸ Wild Encounters\nYou may encounter Min
 ior in its Meteor Form in the wild during the event. You’ll receive 1\,0
 00 Stardust for catching Minior.\nPokémon: Minior (Meteor Form)\nMinior e
 ncounters are more likely from 5:00 p.m. to 9:00 p.m. local time each day.
 \n\n🔗 https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-geminids-2026/
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/minior-showers-geminids-2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:december-communityday2026@pokemon-go-calendar
DTSTAMP:20261126T235103Z
SUMMARY:December Community Day 2026
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Lisbon:20261213T170000
DESCRIPTION:Pokémon from Community Days in 2026 return for an end of the y
 ear celebration!\nThe year is nearly behind us\, which means it’s time t
 o reflect on all the fun everyone had during this year’s Community Days.
  If you missed any\, now’s your chance to catch up!\nThe last Community 
 Day of 2026 will take place over two days—Saturday\, December 12\, 2026\
 , and Sunday\, December 13\, 2026\, from 2:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. local time
 .\nNote: The only difference between Day 1 and Day 2 are the Pokémon appe
 aring more frequently in the wild.\n\n━━ BONUSES ━━\n• Increased
  Spawns\n• 2x XP for catching Pokémon\n• 2x Stardust for catching Pok
 émon\n• 1/2 Hatch Distance when Eggs are placed into Incubators during 
 the event period\n• 2x Catch Candy\n• 2x Chance for Trainers level 31 
 and up to receive Candy XL from catching Pokémon\n• 3-hour Incense**\n
 • 1-hour Lures*\n• Up to two Special Trades can be made per day*\n• 
 Trades made will require 50% less Stardust*\n* While most bonuses are only
  active on December 12 and 13 from 2:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. local time\, the
 se bonuses will be active from Saturday\, December 12\, at 9:00 a.m. to Su
 nday\, December 13\, at 9:00 p.m. local time. ** The three-hour Incense bo
 nus excludes Daily Adventure Incense.\n\n━━ FEATURES ━━\n▸ Limit
 ed-time Evolution Requirement\nFrom Saturday\, December 12\, at 9:00 a.m. 
 to Sunday\, December 13\, at 9:00 p.m. local time\, evolve Bisharp into Ki
 ngambit after defeating 1 Dark- or Steel-type Raid Boss with Bisharp as yo
 ur Buddy Pokémon.\nThis Evolution requirement will return to the usual re
 quirement on Sunday\, December 13\, 2026\, at 9:00 p.m. local time.\nPoké
 mon: Pawniard\, Bisharp\, Kingambit\n\n━━ SPAWNS ━━\nA different s
 et of Pokémon will be featured on each event day—Saturday\, December 12
 \, and Sunday\, December 13\, 2026—from 2:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. local tim
 e.\nThe Pokémon that appear during this time will have the same chance of
  appearing as a Shiny Pokémon as those that appeared during their origina
 l Community Days\, and they may also appear with a Special Background. Out
 side of these times\, any of the featured Pokémon may appear from 9:00 a.
 m. to 9:00 p.m. local time on either Saturday or Sunday!\nThe following Po
 kémon will be featured on Saturday\, December 12\, 2026\, from 2:00 p.m. 
 to 5:00 p.m. local time.\nPokémon: Vulpix\, Alolan Vulpix\, Grookey\, Sco
 rbunny\, Lechonk\, Tinkatink\nYou might even encounter Piplup!\nPokémon: 
 Piplup\nThe following Pokémon will be featured on Sunday\, December 13\, 
 2026\, from 2:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. local time.\nPokémon: Zorua\, Pawniard
 \, Sobble\, Nickit\, Frigibax\nYou might even encounter the following Pok
 émon!\nPokémon: Gible\, Deino\n\n━━ RESEARCH ━━\n▸ Field Resea
 rch Tasks\nField Research leading to encounters with Pokémon featured in 
 Community Days and Community Day Classics in 2026 will be available. These
  Pokémon may have a Special Background!\n\n▸ December Community Day 202
 6 Special Research\nFor US$4.99 (or the equivalent pricing tier in your lo
 cal currency)\, you’ll be able to access the December Community Day–ex
 clusive Special Research. Complete this research for rewards including:\n
 • Encounters with Pokémon featured in Community Days and Community Day 
 Classics in 2026 that have a Special Background\n• 1 Elite Charged TM\n
 • 1 Elite Fast TM\n• 1 Rocket Radar\n• And more!\nYou can purchase a
 nd gift tickets to friends you’ve achieved a Friendship level of Great F
 riends or higher with. To gift a ticket\, tap the Special Research ticket 
 in the in-game shop\, then tap the Gift button instead of the Buy button.\
 n\n▸ Community Ambassador Check-In Timed Research\nCheck in at a Communi
 ty Ambassador event to receive Timed Research that leads to encounters wit
 h Pokémon featured in Community Days in 2026 that have a Special Backgrou
 nd\, as well as other premium item rewards. Find a nearby meetup on the Po
 kémon GO Community Day map.\n\n━━ SHINY ━━\n▸ Shiny Pokémon fr
 om 2026 Community Days\nThis is a list of every available shiny Pokémon f
 eatured in Community Day events in 2026 that are available during this eve
 nt. They are available either through encounters in the wild or via evolut
 ion.\nPokémon: Vulpix\, Ninetales\, Alolan Vulpix\, Alolan Ninetales\, Gr
 ookey\, Thwackey\, Rillaboom\, Scorbunny\, Raboot\, Cinderace\, Lechonk\, 
 Oinkologne\, Tinkatink\, Tinkatuff\, Tinkaton\, Piplup\, Prinplup\, Empole
 on\, Zorua\, Zoroark\, Pawniard\, Bisharp\, Kingambit\, Sobble\, Drizzile\
 , Inteleon\, Nickit\, Thievul\, Frigibax\, Arctibax\, Baxcalibur\, Gible\,
  Gabite\, Garchomp\, Deino\, Zweilous\, Hydreigon\n\n━━ MOVES ━━\n
 The following featured attacks will be available when evolving these Poké
 mon from Saturday\, December 12\, 2026\, at 9:00 a.m. local time to Sunday
 \, December 13\, 2026\, at 9:00 p.m. local time.\n\n▸ Ninetales\nEvolve 
 Vulpix to get a Ninetales that knows the Charged Attack Energy Ball.\nPok
 émon: Vulpix\, Ninetales\n\n▸ Alolan Ninetales\nEvolve Alolan Vulpix to
  get an Alolan Ninetales that knows the Charged Attack Chilling Water.\nPo
 kémon: Alolan Vulpix\, Alolan Ninetales\n\n▸ Empoleon\nEvolve Prinplup 
 (Piplup’s Evolution) to get an Empoleon that knows the Charged Attack Hy
 dro Cannon.\nPokémon: Piplup\, Prinplup\, Empoleon\n\n▸ Garchomp\nEvolv
 e Gabite (Gible’s Evolution) to get a Garchomp that knows the Charged At
 tack Earth Power.\nPokémon: Gible\, Gabite\, Garchomp\n\n▸ Zoroark\nEvo
 lve Zorua to get a Zoroark that knows the Fast Attack Sucker Punch.\nPoké
 mon: Zorua\, Zoroark\n\n▸ Hydreigon\nEvolve Zweilous (Deino’s Evolutio
 n) to get a Hydreigon that knows the Charged Attack Brutal Swing.\nPokémo
 n: Deino\, Zweilous\, Hydreigon\n\n▸ Rillaboom\nEvolve Thwackey (Grookey
 ’s Evolution) to get a Rillaboom that knows the Charged Attack Frenzy Pl
 ant.\nPokémon: Grookey\, Thwackey\, Rillaboom\n\n▸ Cinderace\nEvolve Ra
 boot (Scorbunny’s Evolution) to get a Cinderace that knows the Charged A
 ttack Blast Burn.\nPokémon: Scorbunny\, Raboot\, Cinderace\n\n▸ Inteleo
 n\nEvolve Drizzile (Sobble’s Evolution) to get an Inteleon that knows th
 e Charged Attack Hydro Cannon.\nPokémon: Sobble\, Drizzile\, Inteleon\n\n
 ▸ Thievul\nEvolve Nickit to get a Thievul that knows the Charged Attack 
 Icy Wind.\n…
URL:https://leekduck.com/events/december-communityday2026/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
